# Inspection — Luật An ninh mạng 2025 và vì sao gây tranh cãi
Inspector: independent (did not receive a maker's summary)
Axis: whole
Artifact read: 03-deliverable.md (direct, in full, before opening 03-receipts.md)
Inspected-sha: ffa5b5a3cb54a4f555c6f9a8b337a126c2331b18f6d82edca562b655ec70e366
Verify scope: **Egress blocked — probed once and recorded.** `WebFetch` on
`https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/12/11/vietnam-repeal-harmful-internet-laws` (the single
directly-quoted source in the piece) returned `EGRESS_BLOCKED`. **Zero external sources
opened; zero sampled.** No claim can therefore be promoted above B, and I did not
promote any. All verification below is internal: every figure, date, instrument number,
name, attribution and each of the **19** confidence-table rows was traced line-by-line
against `01-research.md`, plus arithmetic re-run by hand on the vote figures and an
independent hand token-count of the five body movements. Truth-ceiling for this
inspection is B, by environment, not by defect.

## Threshold used
**FIX-IT** = checkably false, unsupported by the fact store, or self-contradictory *as
shipped*. **Minor** = anything I would merely have written differently. Minors are
listed separately and do not enter the verdict.

## Findings

### [result] — the piece is accurate and in scope, with two unsupported absence-claims

Traced against `01-research.md`, the substance holds. Every figure, date and instrument
number in the body matches the fact store at the same value and same date: 10/12/2025
passage; 434/443 vote and 91,75%; 1/7/2026 effect; 116/2025/QH15; 86/2015/QH13 as
amended by 35/2018/QH14; 24/2018/QH14; Nghị định 147/2024; 91/2025/QH15 passed
26/6/2025, effective 1/1/2026; Điều 13; 24h/6h and the separate 24h/3h; 45 vs 58.
Arithmetic re-run: 434/443 = 97,97%, so 91,75% cannot be a share of 443 — the research
file resolves this ("434 of 443 delegates **present** … 91.75% of **total** NA
delegates", 434/473 = 91,75%), and the deliverable preserves the distinct denominator
with "tổng số đại biểu". The number is right (see minor 1 on the wording).

**All six trap conditions pass.** (1) Passage 10/12/2025 and effect 1/7/2026 are stated
as two facts one sentence apart and never merged; the 1/1/2026 outlier is not adopted —
it appears only in table row 2, labelled as a probable conflation with the PDPL date.
(2) The article count is reported as unsettled and explicitly not chosen (§"Những thay
đổi thực chất", final para). (3) HRW is dated 11/12/2024, tied to Nghị định 147/2024 and
Luật 24/2018/QH14, and the next sentence names and rejects the "HRW lên án luật 2025"
inference. The unqualified "Luật An ninh mạng" *inside* the quotation is disambiguated
by the sentence immediately after it — correct handling, not a slip. (4) VCCI is
draft-stage consultation, said so twice. (5) No unnamed critics: I scanned every "một
số", "nhiều nguồn", "giới bình luận" instance. None carries a criticism the record does
not support — "nhiều nguồn cho là gây chồng chéo" and "giới bình luận" both trace to
`01-research.md` and to named domains in the table; the "bundled package" framing is
attributed to commentary in order to *deny* it official status, which is exactly what
research lines 140–146 support. (6) The four instruments are kept distinct with their
numbers throughout the body, and the two consolidated predecessors are named separately
rather than collapsed into "the 2018 law".

**FIX-IT 1 — an unsupported claim about the present state of the implementing decrees.**
§"Điều đáng theo dõi từ 1/7/2026": *"tác động thực tế phụ thuộc vào các nghị định hướng
dẫn **chưa ban hành**"* — asserted flat, as fact. `01-research.md` nowhere establishes
that no implementing decree has been issued. It says only that criteria are "to be set
by government decree" and that scope and duration are "left to implementing decrees"
(research lines 44–50) — a statement about the law's *design*, not about issuance status.
The fact store demonstrably tracked decree issuance where it knew it (it records PDPL
decree 356/2025/NĐ-CP issued 31/12/2025, research line 138); for this law it records
nothing, and the deliverable converts that silence into a positive assertion.

This is load-bearing: the entire closing movement rests on "the decrees are not out yet,
so watch for them". It also has **no confidence-table row** — it is the one substantive
body claim with neither a source nor a grade. And it is at maximum risk at ship time:
the run is dated 2026-09-01, so the law has been in force for two months, exactly the
window in which decrees would be expected to have appeared, and egress is blocked so
nobody in the chain could check. The related clause *"có lên tiếng khi các nghĩa vụ
**bắt đầu áp dụng**"* frames as still-to-come a set of obligations that took effect
1/7/2026; on its own that is stale phrasing rather than a falsehood, but it compounds
the same unanchored-present problem. The piece carries no "as of" date that would let a
reader calibrate either statement.

**FIX-IT 2 — a gap stated as an absence, in the VCCI paragraph.** §"Ba phía tranh cãi":
*"**không có** phát biểu nào của VCCI phản ứng với văn bản thông qua ngày 10/12/2025"* —
asserts that no such statement exists. `01-research.md` line 87–90 says something
weaker and different: *"I **could not find** a named VCCI leader or a dated, quotable
VCCI statement specifically reacting to the final December 2025 text … treat this as
pre-passage input, not a post-passage objection."* Non-finding, not non-existence.

This matters because the piece gets it right everywhere else and the contrast is
visible on the same page: AmCham/EuroCham three lines later is "**không tìm thấy** tuyên
bố nào"; HRW is "**Không tìm thấy** phát biểu nào"; the concentration-of-authority
paragraph is "Hồ sơ nghiên cứu **không ghi nhận** chỉ trích nào … khoảng trống, không
phải bằng chứng không ai lo ngại". Table row 56 also stops at the supported claim
("VCCI góp ý ở giai đoạn dự thảo") and makes no absence claim — so the body outruns its
own table here. The sentence is doing real work (it is the load-bearing support for the
trap-4 framing), which is why the overstatement is not cosmetic. One word fixes it.

Scope: the agreed scope (one statute, main changes, the sides of the dispute, official
rationale) is held; the excursions to 86/2015/QH13 and the PDPL are the ones the brief
licenses as "cần để giải thích".

### [sources] — every table row traces; one row has no domain behind it

I traced all 19 rows. Eighteen name domains that appear in `01-research.md` for that
same fact, with no invented sources and no source credited with something it is not
credited with in the fact store (spot-checked in both directions: vietnamnet.vn for the
server/localisation nuance and the cross-border mechanism; baochinhphu.vn + nhandan.vn
for the vote and the prohibited-content expansion; tsqcb.edu.vn only as the third
corroborator of 24h/6h; Lexology/Mori Hamada only for the 24h/3h user-information
figure and never for the takedown rule; hrw.org/news/2024/12/11 only for the 2024
statement; fpf.org + recordinglaw.com only for the PDPL dates; thevietnamese.org tied
to the named December 2025 article). Row 9 correctly keeps the 24h/3h figure as a
*possibly different obligation*, matching research lines 61–68, rather than merging it
with 24h/6h.

Row 10 ("đầu tư thiết bị" → "quản trị an ninh mạng") cites only *"hồ sơ nghiên cứu …
không nêu tên miền cụ thể cho riêng phát hiện này"*. That is honest rather than
fabricated, and the underlying research bullet does exist (lines 75–79), so it is not a
FIX-IT — see minor 3, where it belongs.

No claim is graded above B. Every one of the 19 rows is B. Nothing is dressed beyond
its evidence in the table.

### [steps] — receipts audited against the page; what they claim is visible

Findings above were reached from the artifact before opening `03-receipts.md`. Auditing
the receipts afterwards: the claimed FIX-IT-round-1 edits are all visible on the page —
the "một số bình luận" attribution is genuinely gone and the paragraph now carries the
gap treatment; the four added table rows exist (cross-border, prohibited content, the
business-obligation shift with its self-declared weak sourcing, and the TVM row); the
TVM sentence is attributed inline by outlet and date; the trimmed clause in the "Về dữ
liệu" paragraph is absent as described. The "19 rows, all B" claim is correct — I
counted. The trap-by-trap list in receipts matches what I found independently on all six
traps. Nothing in the receipts asserts a step whose result I could not see in the
deliverable, and receipts also correct two of their own prior overstatements rather than
repeating them, which is the right behaviour.

The word-count method claim (Grep token dump + line count) I cannot re-run — there is no
shell in this environment. My independent hand count of the five movements gives
roughly 1,225 body tokens plus ~52 heading words ≈ **1,275–1,300**, consistent with the
maker's 1,299 within my own margin of error, and inside the 950–1,300 band on both
counts. I am not treating the band as breached (see minor 7).

The one gap: receipts do not mention the decree-issuance claim or any temporal check
against the ship date, which is consistent with FIX-IT 1 having gone unexamined.

### [plan] — followed; no undeclared drift

Five movements plus the confidence table, in the brief's order, tiếng Việt, third
person, neutral explanatory register, no slogans. The locked lexicon is honoured in the
body: "thông qua 10/12/2025" ≠ "hiệu lực 1/7/2026"; the four instruments each carry
their number. The brief's own six FIX-IT triggers are all avoided. The two published
deviations (Gate 1 and Gate 2 waived) are declared in `00-brief.md`, not decided
silently at assembly.

### [honesty] — the B-ceiling is stated in plain body prose, as required

Paragraph 2 of the body, not only the closing note: *"mọi dữ kiện trong bài chỉ được
kiểm qua kết quả tìm kiếm — không nguồn nào được mở, đọc trực tiếp … nên không claim nào
dưới đây được xếp hạng A, kể cả khi nguồn là báo chính phủ; tất cả tối đa ở hạng B."*
Repeated as a methodology note under the table. No D material; no A leaked in; the two
information gaps that have rows (AmCham/EuroCham, post-passage HRW) are labelled in the
grade column itself as "khoảng trống thông tin, không phải bằng chứng của sự im lặng".
Table-vs-prose holds in both directions apart from the two body claims named in FIX-IT 1
and 2, neither of which has a row — the table never claims more than the body earns.

## Minors (not blocking)

1. *"với 434/443 đại biểu tán thành"* drops "có mặt". The fact store says "434 of 443
   delegates **present**". Without it, the em-dash apposition invites reading 91,75% as
   a restatement of 434/443, which is 97,97%. Both statements are true; the juxtaposition
   is confusing. "443 đại biểu có mặt" removes the trap.
2. Both quotations — the HRW call to repeal, and *"bảo đảm cân bằng giữa an ninh mạng
   với phát triển kinh tế - xã hội và chuyển đổi số"* — are Vietnamese renderings of
   text held in English in the fact store; nothing was read in the original. They are
   faithful, so not dressed-up paraphrase, but a "(tạm dịch)" would be more honest given
   the piece's own no-source-was-opened caveat.
3. Row 10's provenance ("hồ sơ nghiên cứu", no domain) is the piece's weakest link, and
   research lines 75–79 additionally warn that adjacent material in that bullet "may
   partly describe the adjacent Personal Data Protection Law rather than this law
   alone". The deliverable wisely drops the revenue-linked-sanctions half and hedges
   with "được mô tả là", so it stands — but it is the one sentence I would cut for a
   word or two of headroom.
4. *"Hồ sơ nghiên cứu không ghi nhận chỉ trích nào có tên"* puts the run's own research
   dossier into reader-facing prose. Correct discipline, wrong register for a general
   audience — "không tìm thấy" would do the same work.
5. The threat-picture clause (vi phạm dữ liệu, lừa đảo, tội phạm công nghệ cao) traces
   to research lines 131–132 (pbgdpl.camau.gov.vn, congan.ninhbinh.gov.vn), but row 19
   names only xaydungchinhsach.chinhphu.vn and congan.camau.gov.vn.
6. Table row 14 writes "Luật 2018" without its number — the single place the lexicon
   rule slips. The body is clean.
7. Section weights drift from the outline (§4 ≈ 95 words against a ~180 target; §3
   ≈ 470 against ~420) while the total stays in band, and the body sits within a hair
   of the 1,300 ceiling on the maker's own exact method. A fix round has essentially no
   room to add words without cutting elsewhere.

## Verdict: FIX-IT

The piece is substantively strong, in scope, and clears all six trap conditions — the
handling of HRW, VCCI, the article count and the two dates is exactly right. Two
defects meet the bar, and both are the same failure: a claim stated more strongly than
`01-research.md` supports.

Required fixes:

1. §"Điều đáng theo dõi từ 1/7/2026" — *"các nghị định hướng dẫn **chưa ban hành**"* is
   unsupported. `01-research.md` establishes only that the law delegates criteria, scope
   and duration to decrees, never that none has been issued; the deliverable ships on
   2026-09-01, two months after the law took effect, with no way to check. Either (a)
   restate it as delegation without asserting issuance status ("các tiêu chí … do nghị
   định quy định"), or (b) mark it as a non-finding with an explicit vantage date ("tính
   đến thời điểm viết bài, hồ sơ nghiên cứu không ghi nhận nghị định hướng dẫn nào"), and
   in either case give it a confidence-table row at B. While there, fix *"khi các nghĩa
   vụ bắt đầu áp dụng"*, which frames as future an obligation set live since 1/7/2026.
2. §"Ba phía tranh cãi" — *"**không có** phát biểu nào của VCCI phản ứng với văn bản
   thông qua ngày 10/12/2025"* asserts non-existence where the fact store records only
   non-finding ("could not find a named VCCI leader or a dated, quotable VCCI statement
   specifically reacting to the final December 2025 text"). Change to "không tìm thấy",
   matching the treatment the piece already gives AmCham/EuroCham and HRW on the same
   page.

Neither fix requires new research, and both are net word-neutral or shorter — which
matters, given minor 7. Nothing in the minors list is required for a PASS.
